\tag{2.4}
\]

Consequently, if \((P,Q)\) is a counterexample with its \(r\)-component
first, it is almost normalized in Sigray's source/target equivalence class.

#### Proof

Every source coordinate is nonconstant, so \(\deg u,\deg v\ge1\) and

